### ============================================================
### ResolveNow Service Desk — REST Client Test File
### Use with VS Code "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
### or IntelliJ HTTP Client
### ============================================================

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION:
### Switch between LOCAL and RENDER by toggling the baseUrl below:
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1. LOCALHOST:
# @baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

# 2. LIVE RENDER:
@baseUrl = https://resolvenow-service-desk.onrender.com

### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 1. AUTH SERVICE — Registration & Login
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 1.1 Register a new user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john",
  "password": "pass123",
  "email": "john@example.com"
}

### 1.2 Register an ADMIN user
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "admin",
  "password": "admin123",
  "email": "admin@resolvenow.com",
  "role": "ADMIN"
}

### 1.3 Login (copy the token from response)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john",
  "password": "pass123"
}

### 1.4 Validate token (paste token below)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/validate?token={{login.response.body.token}}

### ── NEGATIVE TESTS ──

### 1.5 Register with duplicate username → 409 Conflict
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john",
  "password": "pass123",
  "email": "john2@example.com"
}

### 1.6 Login with wrong password → 401 Unauthorized
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "john",
  "password": "wrongpassword"
}

### 1.7 Register with invalid email → 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "baduser",
  "password": "pass123",
  "email": "not-an-email"
}

### 1.8 Register with short password → 400 Bad Request
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "shortpwd",
  "password": "ab",
  "email": "short@example.com"
}

### 1.9 Validate invalid token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/validate?token=invalid.token.here


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 2. COMPLAINT SERVICE — Create & Track Complaints
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### ⚠️ IMPORTANT: First run request 1.3 (Login), then copy the
### token and replace <JWT_TOKEN> below, OR use the variable
### syntax if your REST client supports it.
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

@token = {{login.response.body.token}}

### 2.1 Create a HIGH priority complaint (auto-assigns to ESCALATION)
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Cannot login to the portal",
  "description": "Getting 500 internal server error every time I try to login to the customer portal",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "userId": 1
}

### 2.2 Create a MEDIUM priority complaint (auto-assigns to GENERAL_SUPPORT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Billing discrepancy found",
  "description": "I was charged twice for my subscription in the month of October 2026",
  "priority": "MEDIUM",
  "userId": 1
}

### 2.3 Create a LOW priority complaint (auto-assigns to SELF_SERVICE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Need password reset instructions",
  "description": "I forgot my password and need step by step instructions to reset it",
  "priority": "LOW",
  "userId": 1
}

### 2.4 Get all complaints
GET {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.5 Get complaint by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/complaints/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.6 Get complaints by user ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/complaints/user/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.7 Update complaint status to IN_PROGRESS
PUT {{baseUrl}}/complaints/1/status?status=IN_PROGRESS
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.8 Update complaint status to RESOLVED
PUT {{baseUrl}}/complaints/1/status?status=RESOLVED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── NEGATIVE TESTS ──

### 2.9 Create complaint without token → 401
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "No auth test",
  "description": "This should fail because no token is provided",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "userId": 1
}

### 2.10 Create complaint with validation errors → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "short",
  "userId": null
}

### 2.11 Get non-existent complaint → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/complaints/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2.12 Update with invalid status → 400
PUT {{baseUrl}}/complaints/1/status?status=INVALID_STATUS
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 3. ASSIGNMENT SERVICE — View Assignments
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 3.1 Get assignment by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.2 Get assignments for complaint #1
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/complaint/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.3 Get all ESCALATION department assignments
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/department/ESCALATION
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.4 Get all GENERAL_SUPPORT assignments
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/department/GENERAL_SUPPORT
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.5 Update assignment status to IN_PROGRESS
PUT {{baseUrl}}/assignments/1/status?status=IN_PROGRESS
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.6 Update assignment status to COMPLETED
PUT {{baseUrl}}/assignments/1/status?status=COMPLETED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### ── NEGATIVE TESTS ──

### 3.7 Get non-existent assignment → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3.8 Create assignment with missing fields → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/assignments
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "complaintId": null,
  "department": ""
}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 4. NOTIFICATION SERVICE — View & Manage Notifications
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 4.1 Get all notifications for user 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/user/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.2 Get unread notifications for user 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/user/1/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.3 Get notification by ID
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.4 Get notifications for complaint #1
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/complaint/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.5 Mark notification #1 as read
PUT {{baseUrl}}/notifications/1/read
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.6 Mark all notifications as read for user 1
PUT {{baseUrl}}/notifications/user/1/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.7 Create a manual notification
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userId": 1,
  "complaintId": 1,
  "message": "Your complaint has been reviewed by a senior agent",
  "type": "STATUS_UPDATE"
}

### ── NEGATIVE TESTS ──

### 4.8 Get non-existent notification → 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4.9 Create notification with missing fields → 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/notifications
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "userId": null,
  "message": "",
  "type": ""
}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 5. END-TO-END FLOW (Run in sequence: 1.1 → 1.3 → 5.1 → 5.2 → 5.3 → 5.4)
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 5.1 Create complaint (triggers: Complaint → Assignment → Notification chain)
POST {{baseUrl}}/complaints
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "title": "Payment gateway timeout",
  "description": "The payment gateway times out after 30 seconds when trying to process credit card payments",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "userId": 1
}

### 5.2 Check auto-generated assignment
GET {{baseUrl}}/assignments/complaint/4
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5.3 Check auto-generated notification
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications/user/1/unread
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5.4 Update complaint status (triggers status notification)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/complaints/4/status?status=RESOLVED
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### 6. EUREKA DASHBOARD
### ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### 6.1 Check registered services (open in browser: http://localhost:8761)
GET http://localhost:8761/eureka/apps
Accept: application/json

